            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure relates to a 5&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;th&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; generation (5G) or pre-5G communication system for supporting a higher data transmission rate than a 4&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;th&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; generation (4G) communication system such as long term evolution (LTE). According to various embodiments of the present disclosure, a method performed by a base station for a wireless communication system comprises transmitting first data based on a first hybrid automatic request, HARQ, process, transmitting second data based on the first HARQ process, receiving a result of reception of the first data, generating third data based on the result of the reception of the first data, and transmitting the third data based on a second HARQ process. Transmitting the second data comprises storing, on a Medium Access Control, MAC, layer, mapping information regarding a relationship between the first HARQ process and the first data.</p>
            </abstract>
